            <ArticleTitle>[Importance of the styloid process syndrome in the differential diagnosis of facial pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>205-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The reported 2 cases of processus styloideus syndrome deserve attention because of their rarity. In the case of complains of uncertain origin and radiating chiefly into the tongue also the processus styloideus syndrome is to be taken into consideration. With the surgical treatment, after having the diagnosis, a well treated illness can be separated from the group of those illnesses in which the main problem is facial pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
